## 11. Conclusion

This project compares two action-value estimation techniques in a nonstationary 10-armed bandit problem.

- The **sample-average method** updates estimates using the number of times an arm has been selected.
- The **constant step-size method** uses a fixed learning rate to give recent rewards continuing influence.
- The **epsilon-greedy strategy** balances exploration and exploitation.
- The average reward and optimal-action percentage graphs help compare the performance of both methods.

**Key takeaway:** When reward values change over time, the agent needs to adapt its estimates to keep selecting good actions.
